  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Late summer heat+humidity to close August and \nopen September\n\nThe latest available model guidance has a fairly good handle on \nthe overall large scale pattern through the middle of next week.\nThe dominant synoptic feature will be a sprawling 500mb \nanticyclone gradually expanding to the east northeast from the \ncentral/southern Plains to the southern Mid Atlantic and\nSoutheast. This will deliver a stretch of very warm and humid\nconditions with temperatures rising several degrees above the\nhistorical average from Sunday (last day of August) through \nWednesday (first few days of September).\n\nThe heat will peak Tuesday and Wednesday with temperatures\nranging from the mid 80s to mid 90s. Heat index values could\napproach the century mark across the south central mountains\neach afternoon as well. Overnight lows in the 60s and 70s will\nprovide little relief from daytime heat. This warm/humid air\nwill also provide ample fuel for thunderstorms as the week wears\non. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Bouts of heavy rain & severe storms possible\nMonday-Wednesday\n\nA series of dynamic shortwaves and frontal systems tracking \neastward along the northern periphery of the elongated upper \nridge will interact with high humidity/very high PWs, strong \nmid level flow/favorable jet streaks, and instability to \nproduce a few episodes of heavy rainfall and possible severe \nweather during the middle part of next week. There are typical \ntiming and amplitude differences of the smaller scale \ndisturbances that will need to be resolved, but the convective \nsignal is supportively bullish for a couple rounds of strong to \nsevere storms and at least localized areas of potentially \nexcessive rainfall. WPC has continued to highlight portions of \nnorth central PA with a marginal risk for Monday & Tuesday \nfollowed by a new, broader coverage for Wed/D5. SPC has \nmaintained the 15% or level 2/5 equivalent severe probs on \nWednesday while acknowledging additional probs will likely be \nneeded on either side of Day 5 based on medium range ML and AI \ngenerated guidance.",
